    "title": "Westbound lanes of I-70 shut down in Columbia after truck flips - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Shiner ,\n2 hours ago COLUMBIA, Mo. (KIMIZ) The westbound lanes of Interstate 70 near the Route Z exit in Boone County were shut down on Wednesday evening after a truck flipped during a crash. Boone County Joint Communications sent a notification at 6:45 p.m. stating that a crash in the westbound lanes occurred near mile marker 133, between north Route Z and the county line with Callaway County. Read full article\n2",
